 Add a criterion asserting the prefix `location /mcp` is retained (structural parse) so /mcp/... sub-path routing has a covering check.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5d","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'The PREFIX location /mcp is retained for /mcp/... sub-paths.'","AC1 asserts only the exact-match `location = /mcp/`; ACs 2-4 cover HSTS, proxy_redirect, and scheme — none assert the retained prefix location for sub-paths."],"finding":"Step 1 states 'The PREFIX location /mcp is retained for /mcp/... sub-paths,' but no acceptance criterion verifies the prefix location survives — an executor could drop it (or the exact-match rules could shadow sub-paths) with no test catching it.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f51db171b8d86bec7","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 1 / Acceptance Criteria","norm_id":"nb141e665690e8597","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A refactor that removes the prefix location breaks /mcp/<subpath> routing without any RED test."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.75,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Correct the Summary line citations to point at the actual trailing-slash URL lines (examples/mcp-clients/codex/config.toml:22 and docs/mcp-client-setup.md:74/114) rather than :18 and :54.","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.31,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["read_file examples/mcp-clients/codex/config.toml:18 is a comment ('# from the gitignored mcp-clients.local.json...'); the url= line is :22","read_file docs/mcp-client-setup.md:54 is blank inside secrets prose; the /mcp/ URLs are at :74,:86,:95,:114,:128,:137","search_files confirms 'https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp/' at codex config.toml:22 and docs :74 etc."],"finding":"The Summary anchors its 'docs point AT the affected form' claim to docs/mcp-client-setup.md:54 and examples/mcp-clients/codex/config.toml:18, but those exact lines hold secrets-handling prose / a header comment, not the https://.../mcp/ URL. The trailing-slash URL actually appears at examples/mcp-clients/codex/config.toml:22 and docs/mcp-client-setup.md:74/86/95/114/128/137. The underlying premise (docs and the committed example specify the trailing-slash form) is TRUE at those other lines, so this is a citation-accuracy defect rather than a false premise.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fdfd85f4ca23ad11e","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Summary — 'The docs point AT the affected form (docs/mcp-client-setup.md:54, examples/mcp-clients/codex/config.toml:18)'","norm_id":"ne126e58bc27e329d","priority":0.44,"reason":"veto:cited-reference-inaccurate","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer or reviewer following the cited line numbers to confirm the blast radius lands on the wrong lines and cannot see the URL being described."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Replace '(docs/mcp-client-setup.